\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan escalates  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  conflict in break with G7.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Wayne Cole   \par \uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 23:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  escalated its war against a higher yen on Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily and openly in a way that widens its differences with other rich countries on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation.   \par \par \uc2 Little more than a week after the Group of Seven industrialized countries called for less market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday took the unusual step of announcing it had sold yen through the New York Federal Reserve Bank.   \par \par \uc2 "The BOJ (Bank of Japan) doing it is one thing, but when it's with the Fed it has a more powerful psychological impact. They're acting on behalf of the BOJ, but that's still significant," said Aziz McMahon, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro in London.   \par \par \uc2 The BOJ and the Fed have a standing agreement to act on eachother's behalf when requested.   \par \par \uc2 "They (Japan) want to send a more powerful message, particularly to the speculative market, which is hugely short dollar/yen at the moment," he added.   \par \par \uc2 The market seemed to get the message, albeit grudgingly, and the dollar had climbed to around 111.50 yen in late trade from an early three-year trough of 110.12.   \par \par \uc2 But it remains well down on the 117.00 levels held before the G7 issued its call to allow free markets to determine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels.   \par \par \uc2 "We still think the G7 statement was very significant," said Ken Landon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Deutsche Bank in New York. "But nobody wants the market just to run away on the downside."   \par \par \uc2 He noted uncertainty over the dollar had eaten away at global equity values in recent days and played a part in Tuesday's 1.1 percent drop in the Dow Jones Industrials Average.   \par \par \uc2 "So this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be aimed at injecting some two-way risk in the market and maybe, just maybe, the (U.S.) Treasury didn't mind that," wondered Landon.   \par \par \uc2 A Treasury official declined comment on Tuesday's wild swings in dollar/yen prices, but only Monday the Treasury had declared there was no change in the country's long-standing strong dollar policy.   \par \par \uc2 Such protestations sit ill with many in the market since many investors believe the U.S. administration engineered the G7 statement last week as a way of weakening the dollar against its Asian competitors, particularly the Chinese yuan and Japanese yen.   \par \par \uc2 In contrast, Japanese politicians and officials have gone out of their way to argue that markets over-interpreted the G7 statement and it had not agreed to let the yen strengthen.   \par \par \uc2 Japan's determination to restrain the yen was emphatically underlined by MOF data on Tuesday showing it spent a record 4.45 trillion yen ($40.23 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from August 28 to September 26.   \par \par \uc2 That was far more than anyone in the market had suspected and boosted this year's total yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a staggering 13.5 trillion yen - or about $120 billion or more than the entire annual GDP of Ireland.   \par \par \uc2 And yet over the past month the dollar has still slumped from above 117.00 yen to near 110.00.   \par \par \uc2 "The scale of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and degree of the move they got in September suggests the underlying yen demand is extremely, extremely strong," said ABN Amro's McMahon.   \par \par \uc2 "It's going to be difficult because it is clear also that U.S. authorities want the dollar lower against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u0030q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
