\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar climbs vs yen on  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 623 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 22:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 30 (Reuters) - The dollar rebounded against the yen on Tuesday in a whiplash move as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during New York trade to weaken the yen after the dollar had sagged to a three-year low.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback remained lower on the day against many other rivals, still smarting from weaker-than-expected U.S. economic data earlier in the session.  \par \par \uc2 Late afternoon in New York, the euro was off its earlier session highs above $1.17, but up 0.61 percent on the day to $1.1662. Against the yen, the dollar was up 0.58 percent to 111.44 yen, after falling to a three-year low of 110.12 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at 1.3172 francs, down 0.60 percent. The pound declined 0.19 percent to $1.6660.  \par \par \uc2 A Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Tuesday the MoF had sold yen for dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, acting through the U.S. Federal Reserve, in a move that jolted the dollar sharply higher on the day against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "It reminds us that the BoJ is still going to be a presence in the market and that they are willing to shift tactics to remind people of that," said Daniel Katzive, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with UBS in Stamford, Conn. The BoJ "felt they had to so something a bit more dramatic," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders say \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the dollar was being broadly punished following weaker than expected U.S. economic data.  \par \par \uc2 Even before the Chicago PMI and consumer sentiment reports clearly undershot consensus forecasts, the dollar was already on the ropes. Traders - perhaps sensing these U.S. reports might disappoint - had already pushed the euro to three-month highs fleetingly above the $1.17 mark even before these reports were released at 10:00 a.m. EDT (1400 GMT).  \par \par \uc2 Before \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was bashed against a slew of major rivals, sinking to five-year lows against the Australian dollar, and down 1 percent against the Swiss franc.  \par \par \uc2 But the dollar's knee-jerk bounce against the yen following \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped mitigate the greenback's losses against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 POWERFUL SIGNAL  \par \par \uc2 The fact that the BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  together with the U.S. Federal Reserve sends a powerful message to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders. "It sends a signal to the market that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has passive U.S. approval," said Steven Englander, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for North America at Barclays Capital in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said Japan's "line in the sand" seems to be around 110 yen.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the BoJ would be reluctant to push the dollar much higher," said Greg Anderson, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro in Chicago. "But the range seems to be in the 110-115 zone. Going forward, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would limit the dollar in the 111 area," he added.  \par \par \uc2 For a long period, the BoJ defended the level of 115.0 yen to the dollar in its yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts, intended to protect the competitiveness of Japanese exporters. But those efforts seemed to end earlier this month when the dollar slipped decisively below that mark.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier in the New York session, softer-than expected U.S. economic data stung the greenback across the board.  \par \par \uc2 The data "reinforces the macroeconomic story since the payroll report earlier this month.... People are now questioning the durability of the (U.S. economic) growth upturn, reinforcing the bearish dollar trend," said Marcel Kasumovich, head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy with Merrill Lynch in New York. (Additional reporting by John Parry in New York).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u002wg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
