\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-US's Snow wants China exchange rate move "now".  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Anna Willard  \par \uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 23:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON, Sept 30 (Reuters) - U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow told lawmakers in a letter earlier this month he wanted to see China move to a more flexible exchange rate "now" and promised he would keep up pressure on Beijing to do so.  \par \par \uc2 In the Sept. 12 letter to senators, a copy of which was obtained by Reuters, Snow reiterated his view that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets should be kept to a minimum.  \par \par \uc2 "It is clear to me that China should move toward greater flexibility in its exchange rate," said Snow's letter. "I would welcome a move toward greater flexibility now."  \par \par \uc2 Snow was responding to a request from Democratic Sens. Charles Schumer and Evan Bayh and Republican Sens. Elizabeth Dole and Lindsey Graham to investigate whether China's pegged exchange rate is harming the U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 The bipartisan group said China's artificially weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes Chinese exports cheap, undermining U.S. producers' sales abroad and leading to job losses in the beleaguered U.S. manufacturing sector.  \par \par \uc2 The loss of 2.5 million factory jobs since January 2001 is a headache for President George W. Bush as he seeks votes for re-election in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 Bush told business leaders in Chicago on Tuesday that China needs to "make sure that China's got a monetary policy which is fair.  \par \par \uc2 "I assured the leaders here that I would work to ... represent the manufacturing sector and all sectors of our economy when it comes to world trade," Bush said.  \par \par \uc2 In his letter, Snow said foreign competition is not the only reason for manufacturing job losses in the United States.  \par \par \uc2 But he said he would "continue to encourage the Chinese authorities to move toward freer trade, freer capital flows, and greater exchange rate flexibility."  \par \par \uc2 Snow wrote to the senators after returning from a trip to China, where he met government officials and tried to persuade them to make changes to their exchange rate regime.  \par \par \uc2 The authorities said they would move to a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system but did not set a time frame.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Undersecretary for International Affairs John Taylor is due to testify to Congress on China's exchange rate on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan, or renminbi, is pegged at around 8.28 per dollar, enforced by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Beijing buys about $10 billion a month to keep the exchange rate stable, and on Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves swelled to a record at the end of August.  \par \par \uc2 Snow told the lawmakers he disapproved of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "As you know, I believe that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values are best determined in open trading markets with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept to a minimum," the letter said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, confirmed earlier on Tuesday that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets through the U.S. Federal Reserve, selling yen for dollars in an attempt to weaken the yen.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has taken a pounding, pushing the yen, the euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stronger levels, since a Sept. 20 meeting of the Group of Seven finance ministers. They agreed that flexible exchange rates are preferable to pegged ones and that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values should be set in financial markets.  \par \par \uc2 Treasury's annual report on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices of U.S. trade partners is due to be released on Oct. 15 and Snow is expected to testify on it shortly thereafter.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u002u8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
