\par\par \b \uc2 Japan escalates  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  conflict in break with G7.   \b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 20:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  escalated its war against a higher yen on Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  openly to rein back the yen against a falling dollar in a way that widens its differences with other rich countries on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  took the unusual step of announcing it had sold yen through the New York Federal Reserve, breaking its recent silence on market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The action occurred little more than a week after the Group of Seven industrialized countries called for more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate regimes.   \par \par \uc2 "The BOJ doing it is one thing, but when it's with the Fed it has a more powerful psychological impact. They're acting on behalf of the BOJ, but that's still significant," said Aziz McMahon, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro in London.   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan and the Fed have a standing agreement to act on behalf of each other when requested.   \par \par \uc2 "They (Japan) want to send a more powerful message, particularly to the speculative market, which is hugely short dollar/yen at the moment," he added.   \par \par \uc2 The market seemed to get the message, and the dollar climbed to around 111.50 yen by midsession from an early three-year trough of 110.12.   \par \par \uc2 But it remains well down on the 117.00 levels held before the G7 issued its statement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "We still think the G7 statement was very significant, and Japan's action is not in the spirit of that," said Ken Landon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Deutsche Bank in New York.   \par \par \uc2 "But nobody wants the market just to run away on the downside," he said, noting the uncertainty over the dollar had also eaten away at global equity values in recent days.   \par \par \uc2 "So this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be aimed at injecting some two-way risk in the market and maybe, just maybe, the (U.S.) Treasury didn't mind that," Landon said.   \par \par \uc2 A U.S. Treasury official declined to comment on Tuesday's wild swings, but on Monday the Treasury said there was no change in the country's long-standing strong dollar policy.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. has expressed concern about the strength of the dollar against its Asian competitors, particularly the Chinese yuan and Japanese yen.   \par \par \uc2 JAPAN DETERMINED TO RESTRAIN YEN   \par \par \uc2 Japan has argued that markets over-interpreted the G7 statement, and it did not agree to let the yen strengthen.   \par \par \uc2 Japan's determination to restrain the yen was underscored by MOF data on Tuesday showing it spent a record 4.45 trillion yen ($40.23 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from August 28 to September 26.   \par \par \uc2 That was far more than anyone in the market had suspected and boosted this year's total yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a staggering 13.5 trillion yen - or more than the entire annual GDP of Ireland.   \par \par \uc2 Yet over the past month the dollar has still slumped from atop 117.00 yen to near 110.00.   \par \par \uc2 "The scale of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and degree of the move they got in September suggests the underlying yen demand is extremely, extremely strong," said ABN Amro's McMahon.   \par \par \uc2 "It's going to be difficult because it is clear also that U.S. authorities want the dollar lower against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u002q6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
