\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar rebounds vs yen after  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Parry  \par \uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 19:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, reflects \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets' reaction to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , updates prices, adds comment)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 30 (Reuters) - The dollar snapped back higher against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bouncing more than 1 yen in a few minutes from a three-year low on Tuesday as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Tuesday the ministry had sold yen for dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, acting through the U.S. Federal Reserve, in a move that jolted the dollar sharply higher on the day against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 But the greenback, still bruised by weaker than expected U.S. economic reports, remained lower on the day against some other major counterparts.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Early Tuesday afternoon in New York, the euro  was off its earlier\par session highs above $1.17 but up 0.6 percent on the day to $1.1663.\par Against the yen       , the dollar was up 0.6 percent on the day to\par 111.46 yen, well above the dollar's earlier three-year low of 110.12\par yen.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Against the Swiss franc , the dollar was at 1.3186 francs, down 0.5 percent on the day. The pound declined 0.2 percent to $1.6632.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Before \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yen-weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which one \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst in New York estimated may have amounted to some $10 billion dollars on Tuesday, the dollar was bashed against a slew of major rivals, sinking to five-year lows against the Australian dollar and down 1 percent against the Swiss franc.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the dollar's knee-jerk spring back against the yen amid the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  helped mitigate the greenback's losses against other rivals.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Today we have conducted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through the New York Federal Reserve Bank. It is dollar buying and yen selling," the Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is quite unusual for the New York Fed to step in on behalf of foreign central banks as it did on Tuesday. The New York Fed declined to comment when asked whether it was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as is the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's standard procedure.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The decision of Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , or MOF, to declare that it had undertaken \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the same day as it had occurred breaks with the approach the Japanese government had adopted for several months of declining to comment.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That change of tack sent an electric shock through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets on Tuesday, delivering a message that the Bank of Japan is eager to defend a new "line in the sand" below which Japan aims to prevent the dollar from weakening against the yen, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Below 110 yen, the BoJ (would have) got very nervous. The BoJ's action allows it to repeg the dollar between 111 and 115. But it would be very hard to put it back up to 115 yen," said Philip Capone, senior trader at Fortis Bank in New York.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan, or BoJ, acts on behalf of Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the event of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For a long period, the BoJ defended the level of 115.0 yen to the dollar in its yen-weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts. But those efforts seemed to end earlier this month when the dollar slipped decisively below that mark.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier in the New York session, softer than expected U.S. economic data stung the greenback, enabling the euro to climb to fresh three-month highs well above the $1.17 mark.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Both the monthly U.S. consumer sentiment report and the Chicago PMI report fell short of consensus forecasts.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That data "reinforces the macro economic story since the payroll report earlier this month ... People are now questioning the durability of the (U.S. economic) growth upturn, reinforcing the bearish dollar trend," said Marcel Kasumovich, head of G-10 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy with Merrill Lynch in New York. (Additional reporting by Gertrude Chavez and Wayne Cole in New York).   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u002ln\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
