\par\par \b \uc2 Dlr spikes vs yen in New York on MoF  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 17:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 30 (Reuters) - The dollar spiked back higher against the yen on Tuesday, and the Japanese Finance Ministry said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market via the U.S. Federal Reserve.  \par \par \uc2 Some New York-based analysts earlier cited suspicions of yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and talk that the New York Federal Reserve may have been buying dollars for yen as reasons for the jump in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Shortly after 10:30 a.m. EDT (1430 GMT), the dollar jumped higher against the yen, to 110.90 yen from around 110.30 yen.  \par \par \uc2 A New York Federal Reserve official declined comment when asked whether the New York Fed was involved in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It is standard procedure for the New York Fed to decline comment on such matters. But \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  later confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  via the Fed.  \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it had no comment on reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 "The New York Fed buying dollars ... that has been the talk in the market.. But I don't know if it's true," said Marc Chandler, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with HSBC in New York.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u002bd\par