\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits 3-yr low vs yen, BOJ talk no aid.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natsuko Waki  \par \uc2 675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 14:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 30 (Reuters) - The dollar slid to three-year lows versus the yen on Tuesday as optimism grew about Japan's recovery, and talk resurfaced the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had resumed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen gains only 10 days after G7 called for more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility.   \par \par \uc2  The greenback was under broad downward pressure in Europe, hitting three-month lows against the euro and Swiss franc on concerns about the shape of the U.S. recovery ahead of key U.S. consumer and manufacturing data due later.   \par \par \uc2  Pro-cyclical Japan has enjoyed massive foreign inflows in the past few months thanks to strong signs of a recovery in the world's second biggest economy. Expectations the Bank of Japan's quarterly "tankan" corporate survey on Wednesday would show improving business conditions added to this momentum.   \par \par \uc2  "Financial markets are ready to accept that Asia, particularly Japan, is in the process of a strong economic upswing. So you don't want to stand in the way of a freight train," said Neil Parker, market strategist at Royal Bank of Scotland Financial Markets.   \par \par \uc2  "We seem to have had two bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today but it seems lacklustre. They are not trying to reverse the recent dollar fall because it is extremely difficult. Risks on today's U.S. data are on the downside as well."   \par \par \uc2  The dollar had fallen to 110.26 yen even as the talk revived that Japanese authorities had resumed selling yen to curb its export-damaging strength although it was pulling out of the trough as New York traders came on line by 1200 GMT.   \par \par \uc2  The greenback also drew little support from \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showing \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent 4.457 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between August 28-September 26, recycling nearly three times the country's entire annual current account surplus. The September total was a record monthly amount, following no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the previous month.   \par \par \uc2  "It might have been a record amount but pure trading volumes in the market have been extraordinarily high," Parker said.   \par \par \uc2  The euro climbed above $1.1690 for the first time since June, building on a two cent leap on Monday, before trimming the day's gains back to just half a percent at $1.1652.   \par \par \uc2  U.S. DATA CONCERNS   \par \par \uc2  Fuelling the dollar's broad-based fall is anticipation of a raft of U.S. economic data this week. Investors are concerned about the long-term sustainability of the U.S. economic recovery given the soft labour market.   \par \par \uc2  "It's an extension of the sell-off we saw yesterday, with model funds and momentum traders getting dollar sell signals as key levels have broken," said Paul Mackel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.   \par \par \uc2  U.S. consumer confidence data for September, due at 1400 GMT, is expected to come in at 81.8 compared with 81.3 in August. National Association of Purchasing Management-Chicago's September index of manufacturing activity, also at 1400 GMT, is forecast at 57.0 compared with 58.9 in August.   \par \par \uc2  The greenback has been reeling ever since the G7 industrialised nations called for flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates on September 20, a move interpreted as a call for Asian nations to stop propping up the dollar for the sake of their exports.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts say Washington was likely to step up pressure on Asia to let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise at an Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) meeting in Bangkok on October 20-21. President George W. Bush is attending the meeting.   \par \par \uc2  Some traders suspected the Bank of Japan had been selling yen in both Asian and European sessions.   \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, declined to comment on whether the Japanese authorities had acted early in the Asian session but said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves had been too rapid.   \par \par \uc2  "The market is obviously worried about the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but people want to buy yen because of a general economy pick-up so the dollar keeps going down," a European bank dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u001ub\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
