\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan sells record amount of yen in September.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara and Yonggi Kang  \par \uc2 813 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 12:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 30 (Reuters) - Japan sold a monthly record 4.4573 trillion yen ($40.2 billion) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in September to try to prevent a strong yen from stalling the country's nascent export-driven economic recovery.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) data on Tuesday showed Japan sold that amount between August 28 and September 26, after refraining from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market during the previous month.   \par \par \uc2  The amount lifted this year's total yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a record of about 13.5 trillion yen ($122 billion) - an amount almost equal to Ireland's gross domestic product.   \par \par \uc2  The figure for January to July had already topped the previous high for a full year of 7.6411 trillion yen hit in 1999. The previous monthly record was around 3.98 trillion yen in May.   \par \par \uc2  "It was much larger than the market had expected," said Junya Tanase, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase.   \par \par \uc2  Tanase said he believed most of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducted before September 20 when the Group of Seven industrial nations issued a statement calling for flexibility in exchange rates.   \par \par \uc2  The G7 statement was generally seen as a message to Tokyo from its trading partners to reconsider its policy of keeping the yen locked in an artificially low range - seen as giving Japanese exports an unfair advantage.   \par \par \uc2  "Even though the amount happens to be quite large, we still believe there will be little effect on the market because the market knows Japan is not as aggressive as before," Tanase said.   \par \par \uc2  Trades for the period are settled in September, and analysts said some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was probably conducted in the last two trading days of August.   \par \par \uc2  The market showed muted reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data, with the dollar holding around 110.30 yen, a three-year low.   \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities fear a strong yen could hurt exports and hit stock prices, key to the health of the banking sector.   \par \par \uc2  In the month to September 26, the dollar fell to a three-year low of around 110.90 yen from around 117.80 - surprising the market, which believed Japan was keen to keep the yen below 115.   \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei share average  is up nearly 28 percent since April despite a 0.1 percent dip on Tuesday, when most Japanese companies closed their books for the fiscal half year.   \par \par \uc2  Early on Tuesday, the dollar jumped to a high of 112.10 yen from 110.67 on what traders believed was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If so, this would be the first such action since the G7 meeting.   \par \par \uc2  But the effect was short-lived and the dollar slipped to a new three-year low of 110.22 yen by late afternoon in Asia.   \par \par \uc2  Market sources said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts on behalf of the MOF, had continuously \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Tokyo market on Tuesday, but they said the amount appeared to be fairly small.   \par \par \uc2  JAWBONING GOES ON   \par \par \uc2  Minutes before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures were announced, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, reiterated that recent moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had been too rapid.   \par \par \uc2  The comments rounded off another day of jawboning by Japanese officials against a strong yen as companies prepared to close books for the half year.   \par \par \uc2  Economics and Financial Services Minister Heizo Takenaka said the speed of the yen's recent rise was a problem and that he would watch its medium-term impact on the economy.   \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki repeated a warning to the market, saying the yen's recent moves were too sudden.   \par \par \uc2  "Recent exchange rate moves have been sudden and need watching," he told reporters after a cabinet meeting.   \par \par \uc2  A strong yen is a negative for Japan's exporters as it makes their products more expensive on international markets and reduces the value of earnings on overseas sales when repatriated.   \par \par \uc2  Toyota Motor Corp President Fujio Cho said on Monday that sudden \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements were a cause of anxiety and that a prolonged rise in the yen would seriously affect earnings.   \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements are supposed to mirror economic fundamentals. But the recent movements are not doing that, and the yen's rise has gone too far," Cho told a news conference.   \par \par \uc2  "If it continues, it will become a serious problem," he said.   \par \par \uc2  Toyota, like many other Japanese exporters, is assuming a dollar/yen rate of 115 yen for the business year to March 31.   \par \par \uc2  Japan's economy grew at an annualised rate of 3.9 percent in the April-June quarter, the fastest growth among the three major industrial economies.   \par \par \uc2  But the patchy nature of Japan's recovery was highlighted on Tuesday with the release of data showing industrial production fell 0.5 percent in August from July while unemployment fell to 5.1 percent of the workforce from 5.3 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u001f4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
