\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slides to 3-yr low vs yen, BOJ talk of no help.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natsuko Waki  \par \uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 12:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 30 (Reuters) - The dollar slid to three-year lows versus the yen on Tuesday as optimism grew about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recovery, prompting talk \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had resumed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  10 days after G7 called for more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback was under broad downward pressure in Europe, hitting three-month lows against the euro and Swiss franc as concerns grew about the shape of the U.S. recovery ahead of key U.S. consumer and manufacturing data due later.  \par \par \uc2 Pro-cyclical Japan has enjoyed massive foreign inflows in the past few months thanks to strong signs of a recovery in the world's second biggest economy. Expectations the Bank of Japan's quarterly "tankan" corporate survey on Wednesday would show improving business conditions added to this momentum.  \par \par \uc2 "Dollar selling is gathering momentum, breaking key support," said Mary Davis, global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at CSFB.  \par \par \uc2 "Japan's economy is improving but the yen's appreciation has huge risks of derailing the recovery. We think they (the BOJ) were in the market...But with the G7 just 10 days ago, Japan might not want to go in to sell unlimited amounts of yen."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar had fallen to 110.26 yen even as the talk revived that Japanese authorities had resumed selling yen to curb its export-damaging strength.  \par \par \uc2 It gave little immediate reaction to \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data which showed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent 4.457 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between August 28-September 26, after conducting no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the previous month. The September total was a record monthly amount.  \par \par \uc2 The euro climbed above $1.1680 for the first time since June, building on a two cent leap on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "It's an extension of the sell-off we saw yesterday, with model funds and momentum traders getting dollar sell signals as key levels have broken," said Paul Mackel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  JITTERS  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been reeling ever since the Group of Seven major industrialised nations called for flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates on September 20, a move interpreted as a call for Asian nations to stop propping up the dollar for the sake of their exports.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say Washington was likely to step up pressure on Asia to let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise at an Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) meeting in Bangkok on October 20-21. President George W. Bush is attending the meeting.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders suspected the Bank of Japan had been selling yen in both Asian and European sessions as the dollar tumbled to session lows.  \par \par \uc2 However Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, declined to comment on whether the Japanese authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the Asian session but said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves had been too rapid.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is obviously worried about the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but people want to buy yen because of a general economy pick-up so the dollar keeps going down," a European bank dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Fuelling the dollar's broadbased fall is anticipation of a raft of U.S. economic data this week. Investors are concerned about the long-term sustainability of the U.S. economic recovery given the soft labour market.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. consumer confidence data for September, due at 1400 GMT, is expected to come in at 81.8 compared with 81.3 in August.  \par \par \uc2 National Association of Purchasing Management-Chicago releases its September index of manufacturing activity, also at 1400 GMT. The index is forecast at 57.0 compared with 58.9 in August.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u00192\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
