\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar extends slide amid talk of Japan action.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Fincher  \par \uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 10:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 30 (Reuters) - The dollar slid to a three-year low against the yen on Tuesday in volatile trade that prompted talk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had resumed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  10 days after G7 ministers called for more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to 110.35 yen even as talk revived that Japanese authorities had revived their policy of selling yen to curb its strength, which damages Japanese exports.  \par \par \uc2 The euro also surged, climbing above $1.1650 for the first time since June, and building on a two cent leap on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 "It's an extension of the sell-off we saw yesterday, with model funds and momentum traders getting dollar sell signals as key levels have broken," said Paul Mackel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 "The exact trigger yesterday is difficult to pin down but the market is now very short dollars going into important key U.S. data, so more volatility is likely."  \par \par \uc2 U.S. consumer confidence figures are due at 1400 GMT along with a regional Chicago manufacturing survey.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been reeling ever since the Group of Seven major industrialised nations called for flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates on September 20, a move interpreted as a call for Asian nations to stop propping up the dollar for the sake of their exports.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  JITTERS  \par \par \uc2 Some Tokyo traders suspected the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been actively selling yen in both Asian and European sessions as the dollar tumbled to session lows, resuming their long-standing policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, declined to comment on whether the Japanese authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the Asian session.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities worry that a strengthening yen could hurt Japan's export-led economic recovery and drag down stock prices, which are key to the health of the banking system.  \par \par \uc2 Yet traders said it may be hard for Japan to reverse the yen's uptrend, particularly as the dollar was weakening across the board. Other traders had yet to be convinced that authorities had taken action.  \par \par \uc2 "The market theme now is yen strength and dollar weakness," said Toru Umemoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley Japan.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think Japan will be able to change this tide no matter how much they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The yen was also buoyed by speculation the Bank of Japan's quarterly "tankan" corporate survey on Wednesday would show improving business conditions and reignite global interest in Japanese stocks.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is obviously worried about the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but people want to buy yen because of a general economy pick-up so the dollar keeps going down," a European bank dealer said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  DATA DUE  \par \par \uc2 With most Japanese companies closing their books for the first half of the business year on Tuesday, position adjustments and hedging activities for the second half added to the weight on the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the authorities had reason to seek a higher dollar/yen exchange rate on Tuesday due to the half-year book-closings.  \par \par \uc2 "It is likely there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push down the yen for the half-year book closing, as it affects companies' earnings reports," said a trader at a foreign bank in Tokyo.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent nine trillion yen ($81 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first seven months of the year, keeping the dollar above 115 yen until early September.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to unveil the amount of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the period between August 28 and September 26 at 1000 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u0011u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
