\par\par \b \uc2 SCHEDULE-Asia Business News at 0520 GMT.   \b0\par\par\uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 07:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Following are some of the main Asian business news stories\par (all times GMT)\par     - - - - TOP STORIES\par     TOKYO - Japan's economic recovery takes a step backwards in\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August as industrial production unexpectedly slips, but   \f28 \par \par \uc2 optimists find reason for hope in forecasts for the following   \par \par \uc2 month and in employment and spending data. (ECONOMY-JAPAN   \par \par \uc2 (WRAPUP 2), expect by 0700, by Tamawa Kadoya, 800 words)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO - Japanese officials step up a jawboning campaign   \par \par \uc2 against a strong yen and traders say Tokyo may have actually   \par \par \uc2 stepped into the market to drive it down ahead of details on   \par \par \uc2 how much it has spent on such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month.   \par \par \uc2 (ECONOMY-\b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -YEN (UPDATE 1), expect by 1030, by Mariko   \par \par \uc2 Hayashibara, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO - Japan Airlines System Corp and All Nippon Airways,   \par \par \uc2 Japan's top two airlines, receive $720 million in emergency   \par \par \uc2 loans from a state-run bank to help them get over the effects   \par \par \uc2 of SARS (AIRLINES-JAPAN-JAL (UPDATE 2), expect by 0530, by   \par \par \uc2 David McMahon, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 SYDNEY - Confident Australian consumers appear to ignore   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  concern over rising household debt as borrowing   \par \par \uc2 jumps again in August, raising speculation of higher interest   \par \par \uc2 rates ahead. (ECONOMY-AUSTRALIA-CREDIT (UPDATE 2, PICTURE),   \par \par \uc2 moved at 0450, by Colin Brinsden, 575 words)   \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI - Volkswagen teams up with a Chinese partner to   \par \par \uc2 plough 240 million euros into an engine-making venture in the   \par \par \uc2 country's financial hub, a vital cog in a massive expansion   \par \par \uc2 plan in its largest car market outside Germany.   \par \par \uc2 (AUTOS-CHINA-VOLKSWAGEN (UPDATE 2), by Ben Blanchard, expect by   \par \par \uc2 0800, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 - ~- --   \par \par \uc2 COMPANIES SEOUL - LG Electronics Inc, the world's largest   \par \par \uc2 producer of airconditioners, says its chief executive and   \par \par \uc2 chairman John Koo has resigned from the company as a part of a   \par \par \uc2 broader shake-up by parent LG Group. (TECH-KOREA-LG (UPDATE 2),   \par \par \uc2 expect by 0630, by Jean Yoon, 600 words)   \par \par \uc2 TAIPEI - Snappy advertising slogans and credit checks as   \par \par \uc2 short as five minutes are turning people like 22-year-old   \par \par \uc2 office worker Grace Lin into giddy shopaholics.   \par \par \uc2 (FINANCIAL-TAIWAN-CASHCARD (ANALYSIS), expect by 0600, by   \par \par \uc2 Rachel Lee and James Peng, 870 words)   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO - Just when the Japanese car market seemed to be   \par \par \uc2 shifting from cheap subcompact models to the more profitable   \par \par \uc2 minivan variety, the country's finicky consumers are demanding   \par \par \uc2 'mini-minivans' and more value-added features, threatening to   \par \par \uc2 eat into auto makers' profit margins (AUTOS-JAPAN-MARGIN   \par \par \uc2 (PICTURE), expect by 0600, by Chang-Ran Kim, 700 words)    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - - - -\par     MARKETS/ECONOMY\par     SHANGHAI - China, the world's fastest-growing major\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economy, is home to Asia's worst-performing share market this   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year - a perplexing weakness that analysts foresee persisting   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for years. (MARKETS-CHINA-ECONOMY, expect by 0600, by Ben   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Blanchard, 700 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL - Inflation hits a six-month high in South Korea,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fanned by high food prices, but analysts expect prices to have   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 peaked and are focusing on prospects for an economic recovery   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in the fourth quarter. (ECONOMY-KOREA (WRAPUP 1), expect by   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0730, by Kim Myong-hwan, 700 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAKARTA - International ratings agency Moody's Investors   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Service lifts its ratings for Indonesia, citing the country's   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strengthening external financial position and improving trend   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in government debt ratios. (ECONOMY-INDONESIA (UPDATE 2),   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expect by 0700, 600 words)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MANILA - Moody's Investors Service cuts its outlook on the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippines' long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  borrowings to negative   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from stable, in a fresh reminder of rising political risk in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the country ahead of elections next year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (ECONOMY-PHILIPPINES-MOODYS (UPDATE 2), moving shortly, by   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rosemarie Francisco, 660 words)    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - - - -\par     If you have any queries, please call:\par     Singapore (65) 6870-3818.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u000kh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
