\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar jumps vs yen, dealers cite BOJ.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Mariko Hayashibara  \par \uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2003\par 05:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 30 (Reuters) - The dollar jumped by more than one percent against the yen on Tuesday on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the last day of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fiscal half year, although it quickly shed gains.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, declined to comment on whether the Japanese authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the dollar's fall after it slipped in early Asian trading to three-year lows below 110.70 yen.  \par \par \uc2 But traders were convinced the BOJ had acted after several weeks of warnings from officials that they were watching the market closely and would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 By 0235 GMT, the dollar had eased to 111.07/10 yen from a high of 112.10 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities worry that an over-strong yen could hurt Japan's export-led economic recovery and drag down stock prices, which are key to the health of the banking system.  \par \par \uc2 With most Japanese companies closing books for the first half of the business year on Tuesday, traders said the authorities had reasons to seek a higher dollar/yen exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 "It is likely there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push down the yen for the half-year book closing, as it affects companies' earnings reports," said a foreign bank trader.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei stock average rose 1.51 percent to 10,384.25 by the end of morning trading, taking heart from the apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent 9 trillion yen ($81 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first seven months of the year, keeping the dollar above 115 yen until early September.  \par \par \uc2 But a Group of Seven statement on September 20 calling for flexibility in exchange rates and the apparent absence of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since then had emboldened yen bulls to test the resolve of the Japanese authorities.  \par \par \uc2 "The market theme now is yen strength and dollar weakness..." said Toru Umemoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley Japan. "So, I don't think Japan will be able to change this tide no matter how much they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to unveil the amount of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the period between August 28 and September 26 at 1000 GMT on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said that Japan likely spent around 2 to 3 trillion yen ($18-27 billion) during that period, when the dollar fell to around 110.90 yen from 117.80 yen.  \par \par \uc2 WATERSHED LEVEL  \par \par \uc2 Had it not been for the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said various factors were pointing to a test of the 110-yen watershed level in the near term.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan's quarterly "tankan" business survey due out on Wednesday is expected to show its headline index rising to, or even above, the neutral zero mark for the first time in nearly three years.  \par \par \uc2 Signs that Japan's economic recovery was gradually taking hold were also seen in Tuesday's employment report, which showed the country's jobless rate fall to 5.1 percent in August from 5.3 percent a month earlier.  \par \par \uc2 But industrial output fell 0.5 percent in August from a month earlier, other data showed on Tuesday, highlighting the fragility of Japan's recovery.  \par \par \uc2 "A fall in the unemployment rate is much more important politically for (Prime Minister Junichiro) Koizumi," said Morgan Stanley's Umemoto.  \par \par \uc2 "So if there had been no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I'm sure overseas hedge funds would have been ready to push the dollar below 110 yen," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro, which had briefly hit three-month highs around $1.645 earlier, stood at $1.1632/35.  \par \par \uc2 Ultimately, traders said, the dollar's fate in the near term depended on the U.S. economic outlook, and Friday's non-farm payrolls figures would be crucial. ($1=110.79 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030930dz9u0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
