\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones News Highlights Top Stories Of The Day  \b0\par\par\uc2 771 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2003\par 14:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par REED SCRAPS NYSE OVERHAUL REPORT; MCCALL RESIGNS \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interim chairman launches sweeping review aimed at producing more extreme changes in Big Board's governance. Lead director H. Carl McCall, who led review now being scrapped, resigns from board, first of many NYSE directors expected to step down in next few weeks.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOTOROLA CAMERA PHONE DELAYED   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Already months behind rivals in offering camera phones, delivery delays will cause product to miss key holiday sales season, making it harder for Motorola to catch up in fast-growing segment.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NOKIA TO CHANGE STRUCTURE   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finnish firm unveils its most sweeping management shake up in more than five years, including plans to restructure business \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to adapt to changing market conditions.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALSTOM'S PAINFUL ROAD TO RECOVERY BEGINS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Embattled French engineering firm sells transmission and distribution business to Areva for $1.1 billion. Hopes to complete transaction, subject to regulatory clearance, January 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAFEWAY DOOR OPENS FOR MORRISON   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. government blocks nation's three biggest supermarket chains from buying smaller rival Safeway, leaving the door open for smaller firm William Morrison, which said it would make a statement shortly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL OFF SLIGHTLY, SEEN FIRM LONG-TERM   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude futures marginally lower, pressured by light profit-taking following surge in prices following OPEC decision to cut oil production Wednesday. Nymex crude futures still above $28 a barrel.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HUMAN GENOME STOPS LEG-ULCER DRUG   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares fall 10% in late trading after Human Genome Sciences discontinues development of drug to treat chronic leg ulcers, setback for biotechnology company's aggressive program to mine drugs from human genetic code.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RIMM 2Q TOPS VIEWS, 3Q VIEW RAISED   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Research In Motion swings to profit of $2.1 million, or 3 cents a share for 2Q, and raises 3Q guidance, excluding items, to 14 cents to 20 cents a share, suggesting BlackBerry maker's momentum gathering speed.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SECOND JUDGE BLOCKS DO-NOT-CALL LIST   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Says registry violates First Amendment as it allows telemarketing calls from charities but not commercial enterprises. Separately, Congress swiftly passes legislation reinstating program after first court knocked it down.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SHOW JAPAN DEFLATION EASING   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's four years of deflation show signs of abating as core consumer prices fall 0.1% in August from year earlier. Government vows to continue working for economic recovery, but there is concern is that recent surge in yen's value could revive deflationary pressures.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN QUAKE INJURES HUNDREDS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Strongest quake anywhere in the world this year, with a magnitude of 8, rocks northern Japan island of Hokkaido injuring at least 323 people. Miraculously there have been no reports of deaths.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WATANABE SAYS G7 DOESN'T RESTRICT JAPAN   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hiroshi Watanabe, director-general of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's international bureau, says last weekend's G7 statement aimed at Japan and China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies hasn't constrained \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "We have a free hand on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CLARK OFFERS FEW SPECIFICS IN DEBATE   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wesley Clark tentatively outlines economic approach a week after entering 2004 race and shooting to top of polls. But rivals focus their fire on Howard Dean, whose financial muscle has made him Democratic front-runner of late.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BURMESE DISSIDENT TO LEAVE HOSPITAL   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pro-democracy leader Aung San Suu Kyi will be released from a Yangon hospital after recovering from surgery but will remain under detention at home, her personal physician says.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US SOLDIER KILLED, 2 HURT IN IRAQ   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One soldier from the 173rd Airborne Brigade killed and two others were wounded during an ambush in northern Iraq, which saw a rocket-propelled grenade fired at their vehicle.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN STOCKS LOWER   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors continue to take profits in sympathy with Wall Street's consolidation Thursday. Shares fall 1.1% in London and 1.2% in Paris.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par THE WALL STREET JOURNAL \par Grasso Hoped Pay Furor Would Ebb   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amid the fury surrounding Dick Grasso's departure pay-off, NYSE's Big Board is facing a number of issues including: whether to split chairman, CEO roles; whether to split the regulatory function; and whether to issue public shares.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHARTING MARKETS \par US Stock Market To Extend Sell-Off   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday 9330.81 is potential bottom for DJIA. Move below that level will confirm breakdown and imminent test of first support.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   ============ U.S. MARKETS ACTION =========== \par DJIA              down 81.55 points to 9343.96 \par NASDAQ            down 26.46 points to 1817.24 \par S&P 500           down  6.11 points to 1003.27 \par 10-year T-note    up 5/32 at 101 12/32 yield 4.076 \par NYMEX Spot Crude  down $0.09 at $28.22/bbl \par Dollar/Euro       up 0.0003 at 1.1487 \par  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 5030 55101  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020030926dz9q0002q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
