\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slows decline amid  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kyle Peterson  \par \uc2 736 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2003\par 17:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 CHICAGO, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The dollar edged to fresh session lows within relatively snug ranges against key rivals on Thursday as wariness about yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  curbed an eight-session rally for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar, which fell to three-year lows below 111 yen this week, was near flat against the euro, whose three-week gain was checked by a disappointing German business survey.  \par \par \uc2 A string of U.S. economic data may help refocus market attention on the likelihood of a U.S. economic recovery. The dollar weakened a touch after the government reported a surprise drop in orders for durable goods, a volatile survey, and a decline in weekly jobless claims.  \par \par \uc2 "What you're seeing is just broad dollar weakness," said Alan Ruskin, research director at 4Cast Inc. in New York. "There's just a lot of caution out there. This is still a case of the market looking at things as a glass half empty as far as the dollar is concerned."  \par \par \uc2 Orders for durable goods fell 0.9 percent in August, the first drop since April and below a forecasted 0.6 percent rise.  \par \par \uc2 Another report showed the number of first time jobless claims fell in the week ended Sept. 20 to 381,000 from 400,000 a week earlier. But the drop was aided by Hurricane Isabel, which closed government offices to would-be claimers on the East Coast.  \par \par \uc2 "We just had a tiny dip lower of the euro on jobless claims, but now it looks as though the attention is on the durable goods orders," said Sean Callow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at IDEAglobal in New York. "It is another reason to kick the dollar lower."  \par \par \uc2 Data on home sales - both new and existing - beat expectations and remains one of the pillars holding up the U.S. economy. Sales of new homes in August rose to an annual rate of 1.15 million units, up from 1.11 million in July. Sales of existing homes rose to a record high annual rate of 6.47 million units in August from 6.13 million in July.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. recovery is in focus as improvement in consumer demand and manufacturing is being held back by soft labor market conditions.  \par \par \uc2 In late morning U.S. trading, the dollar was down 0.21 percent at 111.55 yen . The euro was up 0.3 percent at $1.1526 . The euro was down also near flat at 128.53 yen .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was down 0.5 percent at 1.3429 Swiss francs . Sterling was up 0.22 percent at $1.6624 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar suffered losses Wednesday after oil cartel OPEC issued a shocking announcement that it would cut oil production. The news hit stocks in the United States, Japan and Europe as it clouded the global economic outlook.  \par \par \uc2 The euro climbed back from a dip caused by a slide in the German Ifo survey's business conditions to 79.2 from 79.9, even though the main business climate index rose for a fifth month in a row in September.  \par \par \uc2 YEN RALLY PAUSES  \par \par \uc2 The yen's rally against the dollar paused with the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  near a three-year high notched on Tuesday. Markets had perceived a Group of Seven call for flexible exchange rates as a demand for Japan and China to stop intentionally weakening their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in defense of their export sectors.  \par \par \uc2 But concerns that Japan may again sell its yen have intensified amid a string of statements from officials who insist Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies are unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's new trade minister, Shoichi Nakagawa, warned against sudden moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said authorities were ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a rising yen if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 "We had verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  which drew market attention. The yen is seen as a leading indicator for other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a sharp appreciation from here would prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mary Davies, global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston.  \par \par \uc2 Recent upward pressure on the yen stemmed from a rebound of more than 40 percent in the Nikkei average from 20-year lows set in April, but it fell 1.83 percent on Thursday after OPEC's decision increased worries over Japan's export sector. (Additional reporting by Burton Frierson in London and John Parry in New York).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030926dz9p0018p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
