\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen rise halts on stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  threat.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Burton Frierson  \par \uc2 616 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2003\par 14:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The yen paused on Thursday after rallying this week to three-year highs against the dollar due to wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Tokyo stock losses, while the euro tripped on a disappointing German business survey.  \par \par \uc2 Japan talked down the yen on Wednesday and Thursday, with new trade minister Shoichi Nakagawa the latest to warn against sudden moves after it rose to 110.85 per dollar on Tuesday on a Group of Seven nations' appeal for flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's five-yen rally over the last week was also called into question by financial markets, which pushed Tokyo stocks to four-week lows after an OPEC oil output cut increased worries about the viability of Japan's export-led recovery.  \par \par \uc2 "Following these strong comments from officials, I would say we will not really see Japan allowing the yen to move significantly stronger," said Michael Klawitter, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at West LB. "This is currently what the market is starting to agree on, given also the further declines in the Nikkei."  \par \par \uc2 By 1158 GMT the yen was a touch firmer at 111.60 per dollar. Against the euro it stood at 128.24 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was steady at $1.1497, off this week's eight-week high of $1.1529.  \par \par \uc2 The euro recovered from a dip caused by a drop in the German Ifo survey's business conditions to 79.2 from 79.9, even though the main business climate index rose for a fifth month in a row in September.  \par \par \uc2 DATA FIGHTS FOR ATTENTION  \par \par \uc2 U.S. data fought to regain the attention it had before the G7 roiled markets and a dry spell for releases this week. Markets worry that improvement in consumer demand and manufacturing is being held back by soft labour markets.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. durable goods orders are due at 1230 GMT and are expected to rise 0.6 percent after a 1.0 gain in the previous month. U.S. jobless claims are expected at 400,000 versus 399,000 the previous week.  \par \par \uc2 "The data, according to expectations, doesn't look bad so it confirms somehow the U.S. recovery story," said Klawitter. "Slowly the market focus is shifting away from just the G7."  \par \par \uc2 OPEC's decision was seen as potentially dollar-negative, after it sent Wall Street stocks lower on Wednesday. Futures indices showed signs of a possible recovery at New York's open on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "Anything that dampens global growth prospects is going to damage the dollar," said Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 World oil prices extended a rally after the shock OPEC decision to tighten oil supplies. The gains followed a dollar - a-barrel surge on Wednesday after OPEC agreed to cut output.  \par \par \uc2 YEN COOLS DOWN  \par \par \uc2 Recent upward pressure on the yen stemmed from a rebound of more than 40 percent in the Nikkei stock average from 20-year lows set in April, but it fell 1.8 percent on Thursday after OPEC's decision.  \par \par \uc2 Official comments warning about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise also helped to cool the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said authorities were ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a rising yen if necessary. His predecessor Haruhiko Kuroda, now an adviser to Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, said on Wednesday the yen's rise has gone too far and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 "We had verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  which drew market attention. The yen is seen as a leading indicator for other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a sharp appreciation from here would prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mary Davis, global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030925dz9p001sl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
