\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen comes off boil, euro nervous before Ifo.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natsuko Waki  \par \uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2003\par 09:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 25 (Reuters) - The yen edged away from this week's three-year high against the dollar on Thursday on wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and losses in Tokyo stocks, while the euro traded nervously before German business climate data.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials were keen to talk down the yen earlier in the day, with new trade minister Shoichi Nakagawa being the latest to warn against sudden yen moves. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied to 110.85 yen on Tuesday after Group of Seven industrial nations called for a more flexible exchange rate system.  \par \par \uc2 In Europe, the Ifo index, due at 0800 GMT, is set to rise for a fifth straight month to 92.0 for September from 90.8 a month ago but many doubt this would lift the euro significantly.  \par \par \uc2 "We had verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  which drew market attention. The yen is seen as a leading indicator for other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a sharp appreciation from here would prompt \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mary Davies, global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston.  \par \par \uc2 "Business confidence is improving in Germany, but it's not to say things are turning around there. Europe's recovery is still fragile and lagging the U.S. and Japan."  \par \par \uc2 By 0725 GMT the yen stood at 112.22 after ending the New York session at 111.79 on Wednesday. Against the euro it was also down to 128.76 yen from 128.48 in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The euro stood at $1.1472, off this week's eight-week high of $1.1529.  \par \par \uc2 The shape of a U.S. recovery is also in focus as improvement in consumer demand and manufacturing is being held back by soft labour market conditions.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. durable goods orders are due at 1230 GMT and are expected to rise 0.6 percent after a 1.0 gain in the previous month. U.S. jobless claims are expected to come in at 400,000 compared with 399,000 in the previous week.  \par \par \uc2 A surprise decision by OPEC on Wednesday to cut oil output weighed on Wall Street, putting the dollar under pressure in U.S. trade.  \par \par \uc2 Stock index futures were higher in Europe, indicating a firmer start for Thursday's Wall Street session.  \par \par \uc2 YEN COOLS DOWN  \par \par \uc2 The recent upward pressure on the yen stemmed from a rebound of more than 40 percent in the Nikkei average from 20-year lows set in April.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday the Nikkei fell 1.8 percent after OPEC's decision increased worries over an export-led recovery in oil-dependent Japan.  \par \par \uc2 Also cooling down the yen was a series of official comments which warned about a rise.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said that the authorities were ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against a rising yen if necessary. His predecessor Haruhiko Kuroda, who is now an adviser to Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, said late on Wednesday the yen's rise has gone too far and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 Eisuke Sakakibara, Kuroda's predecessor and also known as "Mr Yen" when he was at that post, said Washington's policy of tolerating \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not changed.  \par \par \uc2 But he also said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not work as market sentiment had turned strongly bullish on Japan and that it was a matter of time before the dollar fell below 110 yen.  \par \par \uc2 "I feel that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the way it used to, which is to defend a certain level of the yen," said Toru Umemoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent so much money on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but criticism from other nations has grown, and because of fund inflows to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has begun to lose effect."   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030925dz9p0013d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
