\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Edges Dn Vs Yen, But Above Overnight Lows  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Lisa Twaronite  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 721 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2003\par 07:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar lost a little ground against the yen in Asia Wednesday but stayed well off its dramatic overnight lows, as market participants pondered where the pair's near-term bottom might lie.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a fresh 33-month low yesterday of Y110.91 - almost a 6% fall in just a little over a week.  \par \par \uc2 The pair recovered overnight from that low, and continued shortcovering in Asia helped push the greenback to an early morning high of Y112.39.  \par \par \uc2 But the dollar remained under continued pressure from hedge-selling, as Japanese exporters and investors who had bet the pair would remain at higher levels are now selling to lock in rates in the new trading band below Y115, a Japanese bank trader said.  \par \par \uc2 Asian market participants were left to wonder what level, if any, Japanese authorities now have in mind as a "line in the sand," to defend with yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Lowering their supporting level to Y110 could be a reasonable strategy for the time being" for the Japanese financial authorities, said Credit Suisse First Boston strategist Satoru Ogasawara.  \par \par \uc2 Letting the dollar "go into free fall is a risk. If it goes below Y100 again, they would have to come up with some kind of reflationary policy," as a strong yen would increase deflationary pressure.  \par \par \uc2 And if Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't decide to defend Y110, CSFB's 12-month dollar forecast of Y108 "could be achieved earlier than we were expecting," he said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y112.14, below Y112.28 in New York late Tuesday. Tokyo markets were closed Tuesday for a national holiday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.1463, higher than $1.1445 in New York. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y128.55, compared with Y128.50 in New York.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.6514, compared with $1.6520 in New York.  \par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants were focusing more on the dollar's downside risks than upside potential, given the amount of pressure still on the pair, some traders refused to rule out the possibility of a near-term rebound. After such a dramatic selloff, some wondered if the pair might have been oversold this week.  \par \par \uc2 "It's still possible for the dollar to recover to Y115 on its own accord," without any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  assistance from Japanese authorities, "considering the significant yen long positions. If the dollar doesn't fall below Y110 anytime soon, some people may start unwinding these positions," CSFB's Ogasawara said.  \par \par \uc2 But the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained a significant market factor Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Many Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders believe that despite the recent Group of Seven statement calling for "more flexibility," Japanese financial authorities still don't want the yen to strengthen too much and will step in at some point to keep a surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from derailing \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nascent economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  must \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen from rising. This can't be helped," said a Japanese trader at an Asian bank in Tokyo. "They can't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  very aggressively after the G7, but they know that a strong yen is especially bad for exporters," many of whom had been counting on a MOF defense at Y115 levels.  \par \par \uc2 Data released Wednesday morning showed bumps in Japan's recovery path. Japanese economic activity decreased 1.5% in July from June, according to the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry's all industry index. The drop in the index, considered a supply-side measure of economic growth, was wider than falls of less than 1.0% many analysts had expected.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro stuck to a relatively narrow Y128.24-Y128.58 range, pressured by Japanese exporter sales.  \par \par \uc2 -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale and Bennett Richardson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020030924dz9o00064\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
