\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen jumps as markets probe for BOJ's limit.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Burton Frierson  \par \uc2 786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2003\par 14:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 23 (Reuters) - The dollar slid one percent to three-year lows against the yen for a second day on Tuesday as markets tested Japan's pain threshold following a weekend call by Group of Seven countries for more flexible exchange rates.  \par \par \uc2 A Japanese market holiday thinned trade, but yen bulls were emboldened by the apparent absence of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tested for the limits of its tolerance after the old 115 yen per dollar floor broke last week.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to 110.93 yen by the European midsession, breaking through Monday's lows as dealers interpreted the G7's appeal for more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies as a call for an end to Asia's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The market has decided to probe the bottom end of what looks like a new lower range for dollar/yen, trying to ascertain exactly where, when and if the Bank of Japan will step in," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland Treasury Services.  \par \par \uc2 "It's a game of cat and mouse. Obviously the trend is downwards, but the trend looks over-extended and there's a danger that the Bank of Japan could step in to march it up."  \par \par \uc2 The yen's rise to its strongest levels against the dollar since late 2000 helped to push the greenback to its lowest against the euro since late July at $1.1529.  \par \par \uc2 However, the euro also dropped to its lowest in over two weeks against the yen, falling to 127.55.  \par \par \uc2 For the second straight day, the Swiss franc also hit its highest level against the dollar since early August, firming to 1.3462.  \par \par \uc2 By 1150 GMT, the dollar had climbed back half a yen from the day's lows after Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said Tokyo was ready to act as needed if foreign exhcange moves were excessive.  \par \par \uc2 "The slight bounce is from the Mizoguchi comments. They're at least trying a little verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the pace of appreciation of the yen," said Adam Cole, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Agricole Indosuez.  \par \par \uc2 "The bigger picture is that markets are going to continue pushing and testing the resolve of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  until we see real \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi, attending IMF meetings in Dubai, also said the yen's recent surge had been partly due to speculative buying and Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance had not changed after Dubai.  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN FOCUS  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said markets were increasingly wary of possible Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though it appeared as though the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not made any discernable attempt to stem the yen's latest surge.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar's breach of the 111 yen level has prompted a bit of nervousness and this has brought some stability to the market," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi.  \par \par \uc2 "The market wants to find out where Japan's tolerance threshold is and my view is that we are approaching it. The longer the BOJ stays away, the greater the risk of disorderly moves that would be in no one's interest."  \par \par \uc2 Japan is concerned that a rapid rise in the yen could jeopardise the country's tentative export-led recovery and has spent some nine trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  already this year.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to exploit the thin market conditions on Tuesday, but there was an incentive for them to prop the dollar up over the next week.  \par \par \uc2 "Their incentive will be that they want to help Japanese banks close their fiscal half-year (Sept 30) on a dollar/yen that's higher because that will look good on their books," said Jan Lambregts, head of Asia-Pacific research at Rabobank in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. GROWTH  \par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow said economic growth in the United States was on a good and sustainable path but acknowledged global concerns about the growing U.S. budget deficit.  \par \par \uc2 He said the U.S. was committed to cutting that deficit in half over the course of the next five years, which would bring it "well below 2 percent of the GDP of the United States and certainly that is very manageable".  \par \par \uc2 Snow also warned that it was unhealthy for the global economy for countries to depend on American consumers for growth and said other nations needed to foster home-grown expansion.  \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council Member Ernst Welteke said he saw no need for further easing of euro zone interest rates, as the 12-nation bloc was on its way to faster growth.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030923dz9n002bv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
