\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Waiting game after Japan says yen rise too rapid.  \b0\par\par\uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2003\par 08:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 23 (Reuters) - Major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were pinned\par to narrow ranges on Tuesday, with bullishness on the yen\par checked as Japan signalled the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise to a three-year\par high after the Group of Seven meeting had been too rapid.\par     A Japanese holiday for the Autumnal Equinox day thinned\par trading, but markets seemed to be marking time as they waited\par for signs of dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par (BOJ).\par     The yen        stayed near 112 per dollar, its wariness\par about rallying in a quiet market reinforced by remarks from\par Japan's Zembei Mizoguchi, attending IMF meetings in Dubai, that\par the yen's rise was too rapid and Japan would act as needed to\par stem disruptive exchange rate moves.\par     Mizoguchi, Japan's top financial diplomat, also said\par markets had overreacted to the G7's call for more flexible\par exchange rates, and thought they would calm down soon.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The yen surged to three-year highs near 111.40 on Monday after\par the G7 called for more flexible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies, which\par markets interpreted as a call for an end to Asia's\par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     While the risk was noted, traders also said there had not\par been much \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the yen's rally so far.\par     "They have been saying this for the past six big figure\par moves (in dollar-yen), and there's been little or no physical\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said a Singapore-based trader.\par     It was likely that while the market was testing the BOJ's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 resolve to curb the yen strength, the Japanese authorities  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 would wait until speculators ran out of dollars to sell, he  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The BOJ knows they will be playing into the hands of the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 speculators. They will wait until the market is nicely short  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 before \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said while the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unlikely to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 exploit the thin market conditions on Tuesday, there was an  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 incentive for them to prop the dollar up over the next week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Their incentive will be that they want to help Japanese  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 banks close their fiscal half-year (Sept 30) on a dollar/yen  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 that's higher because that will look good on their books," said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jan Lambregts, head of Asia-Pacific research at Rabobank in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Yet, he said, the risk remained for a fall in dollar/yen to\par 110.\par     YEN DRIVES\par     The yen was clearly driving the moves in majors and the\par euro was merely tagging along, analysts said.\par     The euro held around $1.1480, not far from the two-month\par highs hit in New York trade. It was quoted near 128.50 yen\par   having come off lows below 128 on Monday.\par     The Swiss franc        was less volatile, trading near\par 1.3530/40 after a spike to early August highs on Monday.\par     Many Asian stock markets stayed weak after Monday's falls,\par which were driven by anxiety that the export-led growth will\par derail as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise.\par     Official rhetoric did not change much, despite the G7.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's new finance minister, Sadakazu Tanigaki, reminded  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 markets on Monday that "in the big picture, the basic policy is  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 unchanged".  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Wim Duisenberg said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 monetary authorities would do everything in their power to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ensure the adjustments in world economic balances are orderly.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow tried to convince markets\par there was no shift in the U.S. strong-dollar policy.\par     And analysts were certain BOJ would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at some\par point.\par     "We do believe BOJ will be coming, because too fast an\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 appreciation definitely is detrimental to the nascent recovery  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and will bring deflationary risks to the economy," said Frank  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gong, head of markets strategy at Bank of America, Hong Kong.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0533GMT. All data taken from Reuters  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2130GMT.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  2002 Cls\par                               .\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.1480   1.1464   +0.14  +10.00   1.0436