\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW: Is Dollar At Y110 More Acceptable To Japan?  \b0\par\par\uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2003\par 21:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jamie McGeever \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Given the violent moves in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates in recent days, only the extremely brave - or foolhardy - would predict with any certainty what Japanese monetary authorities now consider an appropriate dollar/yen exchange rate.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 So whisper it, but Y110.00 is the latest "line in the sand" being bandied about in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market circles as a level Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , maybe reluctantly, is now getting used to.  \par \par \uc2 "There's a lot of confusion in Tokyo, never mind here and New York, on what their policy is," said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at a Japanese bank in London. "But Y110.00 seems to be the psychological level now."  \par \par \uc2 And an options trader in New York Monday noted "heavy interest around Y110.00" from investors buying dollar/yen options with a strike price at that level.  \par \par \uc2 Of course, Y110.00 wouldn't be a fixed rate which Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will defend at all costs.  \par \par \uc2 The joint communique from the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations this weekend calling for "more flexibility in exchange rates...based on market mechanisms" ensures that specific, targeted exchange rates are out of the question.  \par \par \uc2 Rather, any MOF-instructed action in the market from the Bank of Japan in future will be aimed at smoothing out the dollar's anticipated depreciation.  \par \par \uc2 As Japanese officials have hinted Monday, the G7 communique doesn't specifically rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But having apparently remained on the sidelines watching the dollar plunge to 33-month lows of Y111.37 earlier Monday - a staggering fall of 5.5% on the week - the question now is when the BOJ will reappear.  \par \par \uc2 According to ABN Amro, the Japanese authorities are now targeting a dollar/yen exchange rate of Y110-Y115.  \par \par \uc2 "Near term, the market may remain inclined to test \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and establish where the new line in the sand is by taking (the dollar) lower. In this context, we would be wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on any near-term approach towards Y110.00," the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists wrote in a note Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Lara Rhame, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Brown Brothers Harriman in New York, agreed that Y110-Y115 appears to be an acceptable dollar level to Japanese authorities, although "I don't think they're done \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 Most observers agree the implicit G7 call for less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the main reason the BOJ has been conspicuous by its absence Friday and Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Having bought up to a record $100 billion for yen this year to keep the yen at a competitive level for Japan's exporters - mainly above Y115.00, what was until last week considered Japan's last line in the sand - it's unlikely the BOJ has suddenly abandoned this long-standing policy.  \par \par \uc2 But against the backdrop of clear signs of a Japanese economic recovery and a surging Nikkei stock market, the pressure from Japan's G7 partners to let the yen appreciate against the dollar is growing.  \par \par \uc2 "This clearly puts pressure on the Japanese to manage their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a different mechanism than direct (\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ram Bhagavataula, chief economist at Royal Bank of Scotland in New York, predicting an even lower dollar/yen range of Y105.00-Y110.00.  \par \par \uc2 Jamie McGeever, who covers \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in New York, has also reported on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Dow Jones Newswires in Rio de Janeiro, London and Madrid).  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -Jamie McGeever; Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 2096; jamie.mcgeever@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020030922dz9m0005b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
