\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Dlr seen lower still vs yen, but BOJ to stay watchful.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Burton Frierson   \par \uc2 884 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2003\par 15:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 22 (Reuters) - The yen's surge on Monday in the wake of a call by the G7 for exchange rate flexibility shows Japan will accept a dollar decline against the yen, but markets are sure it will still act to counter any precipitate fall.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar's fall on Monday to near three-year lows showed Japan was clearly in the firing line of the Group of Seven statement for its past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the yen's old 115-120 yen range had probably been replaced with 110-115, at least in the short term.   \par \par \uc2 But the dollar's fall was also accompanied by the worst daily tumble in Japan's Nikkei share average in two years, as the surging yen doused optimism over Japan's export-led recovery, giving a hint of what might be at stake with a stronger yen.   \par \par \uc2 While upward pressure on the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain, comments from Japan's newly-appointed Finance Minister, Sadakazu Tanigaki, that policy had not changed was seen as a warning \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still possible, especially since China was seen keeping its exchange rate fixed for now.   \par \par \uc2 "Japan's economy has only just come off the respirator and the country won't want the yen to strengthen too much no matter what the Americans say," said Neal Kimberley, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi in London.   \par \par \uc2 "It would be too great a risk for exporters and the Nikkei."    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By 1130 GMT, the dollar was not far from the day's lows of 111.41 yen ,\par trading down about two percent from late Friday. The euro was down more\par than one percent at 128.30 yen  but up almost one percent against the\par dollar at $1.1472       .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARNING SIGNS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said the G7's statement after its weekend meeting in Dubai that "more flexibility in exchange rates is desirable for major countries or economic areas" clearly meant more falls ahead for the dollar, but many expected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the way down to cushion the fall.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's just a question of time (before they \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 )," said said Michael Klawitter, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at WestLB.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "For the next one to three months I would see it within a 110-115 range. Afterwards, I think it would probably be lower, toward 105."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tanigaki, Japan's newly appointed finance minister, appeared to keep wariness of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  alive, saying he did not intend to change existing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo has sold some $80 billion worth of yen this year, to stop yen strength from snuffing out economic recovery.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  levels should reflect fundamentals and should not be volatile," Tanigaki said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We must be flexible and act when necessary, keeping the big picture in mind," he added.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ABN Amro said in a research note that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets were contemplating the likelihood that Japanese officials have implicitly decided on a new 110-115 range for dollar/yen.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, Japanese financial markets appeared to be questioning whether yen strength was sustainable, pounding the Nikkei down 4.24 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The setback in the Nikkei makes it more likely Japan will not let the dollar drop through the 110 level," said Aziz McMahon, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at ABN Amro.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ASIA FIRMS   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were also on the rise, and markets on the lookout for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by monetary authorities. Dealers in Seoul said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought U.S. dollars after the won firmed to its strongest in nearly three years.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In Taiwan, dealers waited for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appear after the\par Taiwan dollar  traded at a 13-month high. The Thai baht        rallied\par to its strongest level since July 2000.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets also grew more confident that China would allow the yuan to strengthen within 12 months, though even this would not be fast enough to take much pressure off the yen.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese authorities manage the yuan in a tight 8.2760-8.2800 band per dollar, so the market reaction to the G7 showed up in the offshore non-deliverable forwards market , where the yuan premium against the dollar rose to a record high.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't think it is very likely that we will see China reacting swiftly to these demands - at earliest mid-2004," said Klawitter at WestLB.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The problem remains that China cannot reform its financial system very fast.... Against this background I would say we will not see much happening there, which then obviously leaves very much the pressure on the yen."   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As a result the euro is also likely to gain in strength.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although they were less vocal, European G7 members backed Washington in wanting Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to share the strain of the dollar fall seen needed to narrow America's huge trade deficits.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The adjustment so far has been borne chiefly by the euro, hitting exports from the 12 states that use the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Quite simply, if the U.S. is arguing that Asia needs to adjust \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and if you're in Asia holding dollars, you might want to hold something else for a while," said Joe Prendergast, head of global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy and research at Credit Suisse First Boston.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "And the euro may benefit from that diversification".    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030922dz9m008vv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
