\par\par \b \uc2 Asian  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  rally may not herald end to  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By John Mair  \par \uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2003\par 10:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 22 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied sharply on Monday after the world's richest countries called for an end to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but regional policymakers were still uneasy about the surge and threatened to curb the gains.  \par \par \uc2 The Group of Seven over the weekend called for more flexibility in exchange rates, which markets saw as criticism of the U.S. dollar-buying policies of Asian economies.  \par \par \uc2 "The communique is a clear swipe at Japan, China and the rest of Asia's tampering in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," Sydney-based Macquarie Bank analysts said in a report.  \par \par \uc2 The immediate reaction would have pleased European and United States policymakers. The yen surged to a high of 111.37 per dollar, its highest level in over two and a half years, and pulled Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  along in its slipstream.  \par \par \uc2 However, Asian monetary authorities had a different take, and dealers in Seoul said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought U.S. dollars on Monday after the won firmed to its strongest in nearly three years.  \par \par \uc2 Zembei Mizoguchi, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, said the G7 statement was not intended to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap yen gains and, in response to a reporter's question, said the yen's surge had been too rapid.  \par \par \uc2 "We reaffirmed our view on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it is unchanged. Therefore, our stance of closely monitoring markets and taking action as needed is unchanged," Mizoguchi told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 ONE SIDED  \par \par \uc2 In South Korea, an official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea said authorities were concerned about one-sided sentiment in the won.  \par \par \uc2 In Taiwan, dealers waited for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appear after the Taiwan dollar traded at a 13-month high.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the goal posts had changed, but not the game.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think that they would necessarily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less, but they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at lower dollar/Asia levels. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band levels have just been lowered," said Peter Redward, Deutsche Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 Asian revaluation now tops the agenda for politicians from Berlin to Washington because of Asia's massive export flows, China's emergence as the world's factory floor, and a stubbornly weak U.S. labour market ahead of the 2004 presidential election.  \par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  make up around 40 percent of the Federal Reserve's trade-weighted dollar index, so any rise in their value makes U.S. exports more competitive. This, U.S. lawmakers say, should ease stubbornly high unemployment and boost growth.  \par \par \uc2 YUAN SPECULATION  \par \par \uc2 Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lagged the strength of gains in the yen on Monday - the closely watched yen/won cross jumped to a five-month high as the won underperformed - and stock markets weakened as exporter shares came under pressure.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht rallied to its strongest level since July 2000 and markets also grew more confident that China would allow the yuan to strengthen within 12 months.  \par \par \uc2 Chinese authorities manage the yuan in a tight 8.2760-8.2800 band per dollar, so the market reaction to the G7 showed up in the offshore non-deliverable forwards market, where the yuan premium against the dollar rose to a record high.  \par \par \uc2 The one-year contract traded at 2,520 points, which equates to a yuan rate in a year's time of about 8.026 per dollar - three percent stronger than now.  \par \par \uc2 The rationale for Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been to protect export markets, a key economic engine for the region.  \par \par \uc2 That has led to a massive surge in the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves - over $1.66 trillion and largely made up of U.S. dollar assets.  \par \par \uc2 But the policy has attracted European criticism that the euro - which has rallied over 25 percent since the start of 2002 - has had to bear the brunt of adjustment for the massive U.S. current account deficit. Signs of upturn in Japan as parts of Europe slipped into recession added to the complaints. (Additional reporting by Ovais Subhani).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030922dz9m00694\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
