\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japanese officials try to deflect spotlight from yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Tamawa Kadoya  \par \uc2 624 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2003\par 21:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 DUBAI, Sept 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sought to keep the spotlight off its heavy yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Saturday, stoutly maintaining the Group of Seven's basic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance had not changed despite finance chiefs' call for flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said a post-G7 statement urging "major countries or economic areas" to let market forces determine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values was not a specific dig at Japan or China.  \par \par \uc2 "That applies to all countries and is not just limited to China or Japan," Fukui said of the statement after a meeting of G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs here.  \par \par \uc2 "The G7's basic stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unchanged and therefore the G7 stands ready to take appropriate measures if short-term fluctuations threaten sustained growth ... That is why the standard phrase was included in the communique," Fukui told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 The G7 communique contained the stock phrase: "We reaffirm that exchange rates should reflect economic fundamentals. We continue to monitor exchange markets closely and cooperate as appropriate."  \par \par \uc2 But it then added: "In that context, we emphasise that more flexibility in exchange rates is desirable for major countries or economic areas to promote smooth and widespread adjustments in the international financial system, based on market mechanisms."  \par \par \uc2 Fukui said there had been a need to reaffirm the G7's fundamental stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But he acknowledged that the new wording did reflect a growing focus on the Chinese yuan since the summer.  \par \par \uc2 The G7 would continue its dialogue with China aimed at getting Beijing to relax its capital controls, Fukui added.  \par \par \uc2 G7 deputy finance ministers held their first-ever meeting with Chinese officials on Friday to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and economies, and Fukui said Beijing welcomed the prospect of continued cooperation.  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN STANCE UNCHANGED  \par \par \uc2 Zembei Mizoguchi, Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, said the G7 meeting had not changed Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy: the authorities would closely monitor the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and take action as needed.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo spent a record of some nine trillion yen on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first seven months of the year to stem the yen's rise, although it stayed out of the market in August. Dealers saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again this month.  \par \par \uc2 But the yen shot to a new 2-1/2 year high around 113.58 yen to the dollar Friday on speculation Japan would stand aside ahead of the G7 meeting to avoid drawing fire for its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui said some of the yen's rise was due to such thinking but warned speculators that they could get their fingers burned.  \par \par \uc2 "The statement is very clear. The basic stance is unchanged about short-term fluctuations in the market and the markets should reflect that."  \par \par \uc2 Fukui and Mizoguchi headed the Japan delegation in Dubai in the absence of Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa, who was ill.  \par \par \uc2 CONCERN ABOUT U.S. DEFICITS  \par \par \uc2 Fukui said G7 talks focussed on putting the global economic recovery on firmer ground through more balanced growth, a push aimed at correcting an over-dependence on the American economy and because the twin U.S. deficits were not sustainable.  \par \par \uc2 The central banker said he told his G7 counterparts Japan would push ahead with structural reforms and maintain its hyper-loose monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 Based on the "no growth without reform" pledge of Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi - who fended off challengers to win his party's leadership by a landslide on Saturday - Japan would promote regulatory reform, disposal of banks' non-performing loans and industrial revitalisation.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui added that the BOJ would continue flooding the markets with liquidity to keep short-term interest rates near zero until deflation is vanquished.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030920dz9k003ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
