\par\par \b \uc2 ODJ Debt Futures Midday: Curve-Flattening Trades Favoring Long End  \b0\par\par\uc2 620 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2003\par 17:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -- Bonds, Tens Up, Twos Down As Yield Curve Flattens \par   -- Much Trader Attention Focused On Bank Of Japan, Yen \par  \par By Allen Sykora \par     Chicago, Sept. 19 (OsterDowJones) - The yield curve has continued to \par flatten on Friday morning, with debt futures in the long end trading higher \par while the short end is softer, analysts said. \par     Meanwhile, market watchers cited as supportive ideas that the Bank of \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets by buying more U.S. \par dollars and in turn putting that money to work in the Treasury market. \par However, said one, the debt market has pared its gains since the BOJ governor \par suggested earlier today that officials should act "calmly." \par     At 1020 CT (1520 GMT), Dec 10-year notes were up 7 ticks at 112-18.5 and \par Dec 30-year Treasury bonds were up 19 ticks at 109-08. However, Dec five-year \par notes were down 1.5 ticks at 112 even and Dec two-years were down 1.7 ticks \par at 107-07.7. \par     Nearby Eurodollars are not moving much, with Mar down just a half basis \par point at 98.71 and holding in a narrow two-point range for the overnight and \par pit sessions combined, from 98.705 to 98.725. \par     Earlier this month, the Treasury yield curve steepened to almost \par historically high levels, said Briefing.com analyst Ed Rydwelski. \par     "Now we've been seeing some flattening trades put on over the past couple \par of days or so and again this morning," he continued. "In twos, threes and \par fives, yields are actually higher on the day (which means prices are lower). \par And they are a bit lower in 10s and 30s (which means those prices are higher). \par     "So the long end of the curve has been getting a bid at the expense of \par shorter-dated paper." \par     The other theme of the day has been the market's focus on the Japanese \par yen, explained Rydwelski and David Hightower, president of the Hightower \par Report newsletter. \par     There have been expectations that Japanese authorities have been or will \par be buying dollars again as a part of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep their own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par from getting too strong against the greenback, they explained. This is \par because a muscular yen can hurt Japan's export-oriented economy, which is \par trying to re-emerge from its third recession in a little over a decade. \par     "Once they sell yen and buy dollars, they turn around and buy Treasuries \par with them," Hightower said. \par     "With the speculation that the Bank of Japan would be in buying dollars, \par and hence Treasuries with those dollars, we saw a pretty decent bid to U.S. \par Treasuries," said Rydwelski. \par     Dollar/yen has fallen as low as 113.75 yen so far this morning, its \par lowest level since the end of 2000 and beginning of 2001. \par     Earlier this morning, however, Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui \par told reporters that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should be careful not to get flustered. \par This caused Treasuries to pare their gains some, continued Rydwelski. \par     No major economic reports are on the schedule for this morning. \par     Hightower put the next resistance for Dec Treasury bonds at the 110 \par handle, with support at 108-21. In Dec 10-year notes, resistance was put at \par 113-02 and support around 112-14. \par     "It's important to realize we may lift prices up higher than where they \par should be fundamentally just because of this mechanical \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par buying," said Hightower. "We don't have any (economic) numbers until the \par middle of next week. So we could find ourselves way up too high, here." \par  \par     --- \par  \par Allen Sykora, OsterDowJones \par sykora@bendcable.com \par Copyright 2003 OsterDowJones Commodity News (ODJ). All rights reserved. \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 61060  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCS000020030919dz9j000cp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
