\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar sags against yen ahead of G7 meeting.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kyle Peterson  \par \uc2 767 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2003\par 23:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 CHICAGO, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The dollar fell to a 2-1/2-year low against the yen on Friday, sparked by speculation that the Group of Seven of the world's largest economies may object this weekend to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Ministers from the G7 meet in Dubai this weekend. Some in the market believe the leaders may chastise Japan, which has sold its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength and protect Japanese exporters' competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 Talk that the finance ministers may ask Japan to refrain from that practice sent the dollar as low as 113.58 yen on Friday. Many believe that if Japanese finance officials diminish the intensity of yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen will continue firming.  \par \par \uc2 "There is scope for the dollar to depreciate against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the yen," said David Gilmore, partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics. "That doesn't mean that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but that it will do so in smaller amounts and focused on smoothing the movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It will be a managed yen ascent."  \par \par \uc2 Against its major European counterparts, the dollar was down after a fairly mediocre batch of economic data in the last few days, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell below a key support level of 114 yen, down more than 1 percent on the day to session lows. Traders said the next key level to watch is 113 yen and possibly 112 yen over the weekend.  \par \par \uc2 "That in itself was certainly a big contributor to subsequent yen gains," Bob Lynch, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas in New York, said of the technical breach. "On the fundamental side, there is some speculation in the market that the result of the G7 is that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less."  \par \par \uc2 In late New York trading, the euro rose 0.15 percent against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 129.84 yen . Against the dollar, the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose 1.05 percent to $1.1365 after earlier notching a one-month high above $1.1370.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The greenback fell 1.31 percent against the Swiss franc to 1.3676\par francs  and sterling gained around 1.06 percent to $1.6344       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the G7 meeting out of the way next week, traders can look to data for changes to the economic outlook. For the most part, the week will be free of scheduled market-moving news or data. On Thursday, a report on U.S. durable goods orders will be released.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 According to unconfirmed reports, a draft communique from the G7 indicated that member countries would continue to monitor exchange rates closely and cooperate when necessary. The group also hopes to strengthen dialogue among major economies to smooth imbalances in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FUKUI STATEMENT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Further adding fuel to the fire were statements from BoJ Governor Toshihiko Fukui downplaying speculation that Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy would come under closer scrutiny, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The G7 is not a place to criticize specific (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) policies," Fukui told reporters.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He also indicated that with respect to the Chinese yuan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Japan is hoping for "constructive talks" while respecting China's position on the exchange rate for its yuan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has come under fire from the international community for pegging its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to the dollar in an effort to preserve Chinese exporters' trade advantage.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Gertrude Chavez in New York).   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 2020 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par calculated from the levels at 4:30 p.m. (2030 GMT) in the\par previous New York session.\par                      Last     US Close  %Chg   YTD %  2002 Cls\par                               18 Sep.\par -------------------------------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr             1.1361   1.1246   +1.02   +8.86   1.0436\par Dlr/yen              114.22   115.24   -0.89   -4.71   119.87\par Euro/yen             129.76   129.64   +0.09   +3.74   125.08\par Dlr/swiss            1.3678   1.3857   -1.29   -1.58   1.3897\par Stg/dlr              1.6361   1.6173   +1.16   +2.03   1.6035\par Dlr/cad              1.3491   1.3612   -0.89  -13.98   1.5684\par Aus/dlr              0.6714   0.6667   +0.70  +19.64   0.5612\par Euro/swiss           1.5542   1.5582   -0.26   +7.12   1.4509\par Euro/stg             0.6942   0.6952   -0.14   +6.72   0.6505\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All spots  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo spots  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe spots  \f28 \par \par 