\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hovers at 115 yen, nervous over BOJ, G7.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Charlotte Cooper  \par \uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2003\par 14:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The dollar hovered above the previous session's 2-1/2 year low against the yen on Friday, with traders waiting to see if a weekend meeting of G7 ministers would criticise Asian nations' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar dropped through key psychological support of 115 yen on Thursday and traders were surprised there was little evidence of official Japanese activity to prevent the yen from strengthening, after months of suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers speculated Japanese authorities may be more reluctant to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in the run-up to the Group of Seven meeting in Dubai, to deflect criticism from G7 counterparts, but debated whether this would last beyond the meeting.  \par \par \uc2 "There's a little trepidation about taking the dollar much lower now so dollar/yen is stabilising. There could be another run to take it down but there isn't much momentum by investors," said Paul Mackel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro in London.  \par \par \uc2 "People will now sit back and see what comes out of the G7. There's talk there could be official comment about \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their communique which would draw a lot of attention because they haven't really mentioned \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for some time."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading at 115.00 yen at 1150 GMT, slightly below the New York close, after tumbling to 114.72 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro also rose to the upper end of recent ranges, trading up half a percent on the day at $1.1315 but below a one-month high set above $1.1340 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose a third of a percent to 130.08, pulling up from the previous day's low of 129.20.  \par \par \uc2 WORDS BUT NO ACTION?  \par \par \uc2 Britain's Treasury said on Friday there would clearly be a discussion of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the G7 meeting but it didn't think the G7 statement issued at the end of the meeting would set new direction for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 A Treasury official said he would be surprised if there were structured talks between the G7 and China and that Britain did not wish to see a disorderly adjustment in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 Policymakers in the United States and Europe say Asian nations, including China and Japan, are artificially holding their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  down to keep their exports competitive. But a G7 source said on Thursday it would be hard for finance ministers to reach common ground on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this weekend.  \par \par \uc2 Reports, which could not be confirmed at this stage, said a draft communique stated that G7 countries would continue to monitor exchange rates closely and cooperate as appropriate, and strengthen dialogue between major economic areas to promote smooth adjustment of international imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 "If it comes out like that, it won't represent much of a surprise for people," said Ryan Shea, senior international economist at Bank One.  \par \par \uc2 Traders in Tokyo said however that any criticism of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would make it harder for Tokyo to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the meeting.  \par \par \uc2 "It's almost certain \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be criticised at the meeting. Market players are becoming more aware of the risk that it will become more difficult to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 IMF CONTINUES  \par \par \uc2 The annual meeting of the International Monetary Fund continues in Dubai on Friday. World Bank head James Wolfensohn holds a news conference at 1230 GMT, and IMF managing director Horst Koehler holds a news conference at 1345 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The IMF warned on Thursday the dollar may be in for further weakness and developing Asian economies were better placed than Europe or Japan to bear the brunt of its fall.  \par \par \uc2 German producer prices rose at their sharpest annual rate of 2.1 percent in August, data showed on Friday, driven up by a spike in energy prices.  \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council Member Guy Quaden told the Financial Times Deutschland newspaper there was little reason to lower euro zone interest rates, and even less reason to raise them.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030919dz9j009na\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
