\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steadies before G7, eyes on Japan.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2003\par 09:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The dollar steadied against the yen on Friday after its break below the key psychological 115 level in the previous session prompted views that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is taking a more relaxed stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers speculated that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities would soften their stance in the run-up to the weekend Group of Seven meeting in Dubai, to deflect criticism from counterparts.  \par \par \uc2 The euro also stabilised at the upper end of recent ranges against the dollar, as markets looked to the meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors on Saturday for direction.  \par \par \uc2 "We have had this speculative move (in dollar/yen) in the run-up to the meeting and we may see another go at that level today," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi.  \par \par \uc2 "We won't see much from the official statement from the G7, but we may again see Treasury Secretary Snow asking Asian central banks to stand back from the market."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading at 115.24/25 yen at 0720 GMT, little changed from the New York close, after falling to a 2-1/2 year low of 114.72 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was moving sideways against the dollar, trading at $1.1261/65, barely changed from Thursday's close.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steadied at 129.80/81.  \par \par \uc2 Market players are now starting to think Japan may be forced to curtail yen-selling after the G7, where its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be attacked as an unfair way of supporting exporters to ensure a recent pickup in the economy is maintained.  \par \par \uc2 "It's almost certain \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be criticised at the meeting," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JP Morgan Chase in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 "Market players are becoming more aware of the risk that it will become more difficult (for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," Sasaki added.  \par \par \uc2 A G7 source said on Thursday it would be difficult for G7 finance ministers to reach common ground on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this weekend.  \par \par \uc2 Reports of a draft communique, which could not be confirmed at this stage, said the communique stated G7 countries would continue to monitor exchange rates closely and cooperate as appropriate, and strengthen dialogue between major economic areas to promote smooth adjustment of international imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 IMF CONTINUES  \par \par \uc2 The annual meeting of the International Monetary Fund continues in Dubai on Friday. World Bank head James Wolfensohn holds a news conference at 1230 GMT, and IMF managing director Horst Koehler holds a news conference at 1345 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The IMF warned on Thursday the dollar may be in for further weakness and developing Asian economies were better placed than Europe or Japan to bear the brunt of its fall.  \par \par \uc2 German producer prices rose at their sharpest annual rate of 2.1 percent in August, data showed on Friday, driven up by a spike in energy prices.  \par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council Member Guy Quaden told the Financial Times Deutschland newspaper there was little reason to lower euro zone interest rates, and even less reason to raise them.  \par \par \uc2 BROKEN LINE IN SAND  \par \par \uc2 Traders were stunned to see the dollar break below the closely watched level of 115 yen on Thursday, seen as a point at which Tokyo authorities would form a rock-solid defence.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese exporters, who have dollars earned overseas that they wish to convert into yen, are getting nervous as to whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which they had long counted on, will continue in the future.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo spent some nine trillion yen ($77.6 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the first seven months of the year, then stayed out of the market in August. But it is thought to have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again this month to stem the yen's latest rise.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030919dz9j005nb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
