\par\par \b \uc2  EUROPEAN MORNING BRIEFING: Stocks Take A Break \b0\par\par\uc2 1,631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2003\par 06:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US SUMMARY: Stocks Lower; NYSE Boss Grasso Quits\par DJIA          9545.65    loss 21.69     dn 0.2%\par NASDAQ        1883.10    loss 4.15      dn 0.2%\par S&P 500       1025.97    loss 3.35      dn 0.3%\par Dow Future    9551.00    loss 12.00     up 0.1%\par NASDAQ Future 1380.50    unchanged         0.0%\par S&P Future    1026.75    loss 0.50      dn 0.1%\par 10-Yr US Treasury: 4.16% down 0.11\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- Wall Street drifted lower Wednesday after a mixed housing report and a disappointing outlook from DuPont gave investors incentives to cash in profits after the previous session's big advance. Prices of Treasurys rallied. \par \par \uc2  STOCKS: Analysts said many investors were taking a wait-and-see attitude before the upcoming earnings period. Trading also was choppy due to technical factors in advance of Friday's quadruple-witching day, the quarterly expiration of index futures and options as well as individual stock futures and options. \par \par \uc2  The Commerce Department reported that builders started work on 1.82 million housing units at a seasonally adjusted annual rate last month. Analysts were predicting a level of 1.89 million units. \par \par \uc2  New York Stock Exchange chairman Dick Grasso resigned Wednesday amid rising fury over his $139.5 million pay package, his 36-year career ruined by cries that he made too much money running the world's richest financial market. \par \par \uc2  BONDS: U.S. Treasury prices rose on the expectation that the Federal Reserve will keep rates low into the second half of next year. \par \par \uc2  However, the present flattening in the curve is "a buying opportunity as the long-term trend for the curve is one of continued steepness," said William Strazzullo, market strategist at State Street in Boston. That is based on accommodative monetary policy for an extended period of time ultimately sparking higher inflation and a growing budget deficit leading to large amounts of future Treasury supply, he said. \par \par \uc2  Brian Edmonds, global head of Treasury trading at Banc of America Securities in New York said the market will likely stay in a narrow band in the next few sessions, with the 10-year note yield seen between 4.10% and 4.45%. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Hurricane Isabel closed in on North Carolina's Outer Banks on with 169 kph winds and the potential for up to 30 centimeters of rain, threatening to cause ruinous flooding across a huge swath of the already soggy East. \par \par \uc2  In America's capital, federal and district offices were ordered closed and Congress canceled votes so members could return home. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ASIAN SUMMARY: Tokyo Shares Dip; Japan Eyes $1B Iraq Aid\par USD-Yen             116.01       loss  0.18    dn 0.1%\par AUD-USD             0.6644       loss  0.0010  dn 0.2%\par Nikkei 225          10937.77     loss  52.34   dn 0.5%\par Hang Seng           11051.39     loss  88.66   dn 0.9%\par JGB Yield           1.4050% down 0.0200\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Tokyo stocks fell Thursday morning as investors\par took profits from recent gains, while the market also was discouraged by\par Wall Street's overnight losses.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The weak dollar prompted selling of high-technology and exporter blue\par chips, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Electronics giants Fujitsu, Matsushita Electric and Sony, and\par automakers Honda, Nissan and Toyota were lower Thursday morning.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the dollar continued its downtrend from overnight\par trading in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan is planning to contribute at least US$1 billion next year to\par reconstruction efforts in Iraq, a report in Nihon Keizai financial\par newspaper said Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Group of Seven (G-7) industrial countries, whose finance ministers\par and central bankers meet Saturday in Dubai, are considering an\par unofficial meeting with representatives from China, the Nihon Keizai\par Shimbun said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the reason China should avoid revaluing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , according to\par the head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading for giant banking group HSBC\par Holdings PLC, is simple: it might not rise. "Why would you want to be\par buying this \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ? It's not a surefire, slam-dunk," said Stuart\par Gulliver, chief executive of corporate, investment banking and markets\par for the London-based giant.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPEAN OUTLOOK: Stocks Seen Lower As Bonds Grab Spotlight\par Euro-USD            1.1274      loss  0.0012  dn 0.1%\par Stlg-USD            1.6075      loss  0.0018  dn 0.1%\par USD-Franc           1.3808      gain  0.0016  up 0.1%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ZURICH (Dow Jones)--European share prices may open slightly weaker\par while prices of government bonds rise with the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par STOCKS: European shares are expected to open slightly lower after Wall\par Street failed to continue its rally over the Federal Reserve's decision\par to leave key interest rates at a 45-year low.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Peter Dixon, economist at Commerzbank, said that the Fed's decision\par helped reassure markets but also highlighted the underperformance in the\par U.S. jobs market. "Persistently weak initial claims data and employment\par figures could prove a stumbling block for equity markets in the weeks\par ahead," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the U.S., a Minnesota district court denied giving class-action\par status to lawsuits against Bayer AG (BAY) over its Baycol cholesterol\par drug, which has been linked to a number of deaths.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BONDS: Euro-zone government bond may extend price gains after the\par rally in U.S. Treasurys overnight and the rise in the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market participants will be watching data from the U.S. Thursday, with\par the September Philadelphia Fed business index and initial jobless claims\par data due.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Last week's (jobless claims) reading was distorted because of the\par Labor day weekend, so it should be quite interesting to get a clean\par reading...given all the talk about jobless recovery," said Jason\par Simpson, analyst with ABN Amro in London.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : The euro opens the session around $1.1275, and needs to get\par over $1.1320 to have a shot at $1.1500.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday got a lift from massive buying of\par sterling after a strong suggestion from the Bank of England that U.K.\par interest rates could be raised soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar remained well supported against the yen, however, even\par though there was no overt yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from Japanese\par monetary authorities, according to dealers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rather, the ever-present threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , to keep the yen at a competitive\par level for Japanese exporters, was enough to avert heavier dollar\par weakness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Spread differentials that had favored the U.S. over the euro zone not\par too long ago are now equal," and could favor the euro in the near term,\par said Tim Mazanec, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Investors Bank & Trust.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CALENDAR: Thursday, Sep 18: EU Trade; US Jobless, Philly Fed\par ET/GMT\par 0245/0645 France       July Current Account\par 0300/0700 E.U.         ECB meetings\par 0430/0830 U.K.         Bank of England governor\par 0430/0830 U.K.         August PSCNR (seen GBP3.0B)\par 0430/0830 U.K.         Retail sales (seen -0.2% MM, +3.7% YY)\par 0430/0830 U.K.         August M4 Money Supply (seen 0.5% MM)\par 0600/1000 E.U.         July Trade (seen EUR8B; last EUR5.4B)\par 0600/1000 U.K.         CBI Industrial trends\par 0830/1230 U.S.         Initial Jobless Claims for September 13\par 1000/1400 U.S.         August Leading Indicators\par 1000/1400 U.S.         DJ-BTM Business Barometer for September\par 1200/1600 U.S.         Sept Philadelphia Fed Business Index\par 1400/1800 U.S.         August Federal Open Market Committee\par 1630/2030 U.S.         Money Supply\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Dennis Baker; Dow Jones Newswires; 41-1-212-2181;\par dennis.baker@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Morrisons (U.MRW): 1H Earnings\par Consensus pre-exceptional pretax profit (DJ, 4 analysts): GBP128M\par (GBP114.5M)\par Note: Same-store sales seen up between 7.7%-9%, having benefitted from\par hot summer. Results will mark beginning of a busy period for the\par retailer; Safeway (U.SFW) bid announcement imminent.\par Next (U.NXT): 1H Earnings\par Consensus pretax profit (DJ, 3 analysts): GBP116.9M (GBP116M)\par Note: 1H numbers to be held back by share buyback program and late\par timing of summer sale. Current trading seen soft due to hot weather\par and tough comparatives last year, though range improvements should\par point to improving trend, say analysts.\par Antisoma (U.ASM): FY Earnings\par Consensus pretax loss (Hemscott, 3 analysts): GBP5.34M (GBP13.2M loss)\par Note: EPS loss is pegged at 1.8 pence, compared with 10.8 pence loss in\par 2002. Analysts will be looking for an update on R1549, lead drug for\par ovarian cancer, Phase III trial of which is expected to finish six\par months earlier than expected.\par Havas (F.HAV): 1H Earnings\par Note: The company said in Jul that 1H revenues fell 18.8% to EUR835.6M\par from EUR992.7M last year.\par Oberthur CS (F.OCS): 1H Earnings\par Note: The company said in Jul that H1 revenues fell 7.6% to EUR200.9M\par from EUr217.6M last year.\par Alvis (U.USH): 1H Earnings\par Atlantic Global (U.AGO): 1H Earnings\par Capital & Regional (U.CAL): 1H Earnings\par Carnival (U.CCL): 3Q Earnings\par Note: Carnival Corp & PLC Thursday 1300 GMT to report third quarter\par earnings per share of $0.88, up 3.5% from $0.85, according to a\par consensus of three analysts. US demand for domestic cruises remained\par strong over summer, says Morgan Stanley's Jamie Rollo. Carnival may\par revise its expectations for a 4%-to-6% yield decline from 2H onwards\par but no yield or EPS guidance expected for 2004.\par Chime Communications (U.CMC): 1H Earnings\par Codascisys (U.CSC): 1H Earnings\par Esprit Holdings (H.ESP): FY Earnings\par Kiln (U.KIN): 1H Earnings\par Servicepower Technologies (U.SVP): 1H Earnings\par Venture Production (U.VPC): 1H Earnings\par Yoomedia (U.YOO): 1H Earnings\par Urbium (U.URM): 1H Earnings\par Colefax (U.CFX): AGM\par Heiton Group (U.HIT): AGM\par Henderson Elec&Gen (U.HEG): AGM\par International Greetings (U.IHI): EGM\par Reflec (U.RFL): AGM\par Templeton Emerging (U.TEM): AGM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 18-09-03 0501GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1011 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030918dz9i0007l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pi