\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar falls vs yen - traders test the BoJ.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kyle Peterson  \par \uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2003\par 19:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comment, changes byline, dateline; previous NEW YORK)  \par \par \uc2 CHICAGO, Sept 18 (Reuters) - The dollar slumped against the yen on Thursday, shedding more than 1 percent to hit a 2-1/2-year low as traders challenged the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to undertake yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar later recovered some losses on yen profit-taking and edged back above 115 yen. The greenback also retraced against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was trading higher on the day against the euro and the Swiss franc.  \par \par \uc2 The market's focus on the dollar/yen axis was intense and left considerations of fairly positive U.S. economic data in the shade. Traders dared the BoJ to redefine the "line in the sand," or level at which Japan is willing to tolerate yen strength, as the Group of Seven meeting in Dubai gets underway.  \par \par \uc2 "The underlying flows remain quite supportive (for the yen)," said Daniel Katzive, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS in Stamford, Connecticut. "Absent official bids, the tendency for dollar/yen is going to be lower."   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By early afternoon in New York the dollar was down 0.74 percent to\par 115.16 yen  after slipping to a 2-1/2 year low of 114.77 yen. The euro\par fell 1.02 percent on the day to 129.64 yen           against the\par Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't think the BoJ is in the market, although it is a possibility they may come in later," said Tommy Molloy, a trader at Bank Leumi in New York. "The bounce we saw above 115 yen was just prudent short-covering, more than anything else," he added.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Both BoJ and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials in New York declined to comment when asked whether the BoJ was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets. The BoJ, which acts on behalf of the ministry in the case of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sells yen for dollars when \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market in an effort to protect \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's competitive trade advantage.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Molloy expects investors to test the 115 yen level again during the day, taking advantage of the BoJ's seeming reluctance to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the risk of public rebuke from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's G7 partners.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets are wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect a fragile export-led recovery after record levels of official yen sales this year. But traders are reluctant to be short yen amid a Tokyo equities rally that has pushed shares to 15-month peaks.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Even though we have seen a very conspicuous lack of BoJ action, it still takes a very gutsy trader to short dollar/yen and ride it all the way down," said Lara Rhame, senior economist with Brown Brothers Harriman in New York.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was down 0.30 percent on the day at $1.1252 . Sterling gained 0.37 percent against the dollar to $1.6163 , continuing to benefit from expectations of an early monetary policy tightening by the Bank of England.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. DATA  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The focus on the yen and G7 meeting overshadowed mostly firmer U.S. economic data.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Initial applications for weekly U.S. jobless benefits fell to 399,000, below the widely watched 400,000 mark and offering the dollar a temporary, but fleeting respite.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This was followed by a rise in a key U.S. economic forecasting gauge for August - the index of leading indicators - suggesting economic growth will strengthen further in the second half of the year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But this was followed by a weaker-than-expected Philadelphia Fed survey, an indicator of mid-Atlantic manufacturing activity. The index declined to 14.6, compared with expectations of a 17.3 reading.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "More than anything else, the dollar is being affected by the G7 meeting," said David Durrant, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Bank Julius Baer in New York.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In terms of the jobless data, 399,000 and expectations of 410,000 were not that significant. What we should look at is the continuing claims, which are still rising," he said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030918dz9i003he\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
