\par\par \b \uc2 Traders suspect BoJ did not support dollar vs yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2003\par 16:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 18 (Reuters) - The dollar sagged below a critical 'line in the sand' against the yen of 115.00 on Thursday, a 2-1/2 year low, with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently avoiding yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  initially, traders in New York and London said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar tumbled to session lows, slipping swiftly below 115.00 yen to ultimately reach 114.77 yen . Although the greenback managed a fleeting bounce back up to 115.20 yen, it remained under pressure as investors tested the Bank of Japan's resolve to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from gaining too much value.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts and traders said they suspected the BoJ was not actively trying to support the dollar, especially given top officials from the Group of Seven major industrialized nations are meeting in Dubai this week. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thought to be a hot topic, though not likely to show up in official documents.  \par \par \uc2 The BoJ was seen refraining from supporting dollar/yen bid on Thursday, causing a "huge round of stop-loss selling below 115.00 yen," with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  options-related selling occurring at that level as well, said Mike King, trader at Commerzbank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "BoJ appears to have pulled the bid as big Japanese names are doing a lot of the aggressive selling, perhaps because of the G7 meeting when one of the largely discussed topics is expected to be \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation," said King.  \par \par \uc2 Officials in New York at both the Bank of Japan and Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on Thursday when asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 As the dollar slips against the yen, "we are seeing speculative names: the BoJ is not fighting back," said Michael Woolfolk, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with the Bank of New York."  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan acts on behalf of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the case of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government wants to curb the appreciation of the yen in order to protect the competitiveness of Japanese exporters.  \par \par \uc2 "We have not seen any sort of quasi official bids in the market yet," said Aziz McMahon, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro in London.  \par \par \uc2 But McMahon added that as the dollar comes under more pressure against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and more market positions bet that the yen will continue to appreciate, "conditions are increasingly ripe for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".  \par \par \uc2 "That doesn't mean they (the BOJ) won't be there. Speculation would be that they (the BOJ) don't want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the weekend (meeting of the Group of Seven)," McMahon added.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020030918dz9i002ue\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
